(also under https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.12/6.12.1/submodules/ while 6.12.1 is current). On
request, the YAKBD maintainers provide these same source archives, and the source of any other LGPL component a
package of the editor contains: open an issue in this repository or contact the maintainers through
https://github.com/yakbd.

Qt modules shipped with the editor (all "LGPL-3.0-only" options of Qt's dual licensing, as stated in the software
bill of materials inside each Qt archive): Qt Core, Qt Gui, Qt DBus (Linux), Qt Network, Qt OpenGL, Qt Svg, Qt Qml,
Qt QmlMeta, Qt QmlModels, Qt QmlWorkerScript, Qt Quick, Qt Quick Layouts, Qt Quick Shapes, Qt Quick Effects,
Qt Quick Templates 2, Qt Quick Controls 2 (with the Basic, Fusion and FluentWinUI3 styles; on Windows also the
Windows style and Qt Quick Native Style, on macOS the macOS style and Qt Quick Native Style), Qt Quick Dialogs 2
(with its utilities and Qt Quick implementation), Qt Labs FolderListModel, and on Linux Qt Wayland Client,
Qt WlShellIntegration and Qt XcbQpa, with the Qt plugins they load (platforms, platform themes, image formats, icon
engines, TLS, Wayland and xcb integrations). The Qt tools used to build the editor (moc, rcc, qmlcachegen and
others) are covered by the GPL with the Qt GPL exception, which covers their output.

Qt bundles third-party code under its own licences; the list is in each Qt module's documentation
(https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/licenses-used-in-qt.html) and in the SBOM files of the Qt archives.

