Visual C++ runtime (Windows packages)
-------------------------------------
The Windows builds (x64 and arm64) are made with Microsoft Visual C++ (Visual Studio 2022) and ship its runtime
DLLs (vcruntime140*.dll, msvcp140*.dll, concrt140.dll and the others of the toolset's Microsoft.VC*.CRT folder) next to
the editor. They are Microsoft's redistributable files, distributed under the Visual Studio licence terms that
allow their redistribution with an application; they are not open source.

AppImage runtime (Linux AppImage only)
--------------------------------------
The AppImage file begins with the AppImage type 2 runtime, release 20251108 (https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime),
MIT licence (third_party/licenses/AppImage-type2-runtime-MIT.txt). The runtime is a static program with these
libraries built in, each under its own licence:

    libfuse 3.15.0, with the runtime's patch patches/libfuse/mount.c.diff   LGPL-2.1 (third_party/licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt)
    squashfuse 0.5.2                                                        BSD-2-Clause
    zstd                                                                    BSD-3-Clause (dual BSD/GPLv2; used as BSD)
    zlib                                                                    zlib
    mimalloc                                                                MIT
    musl libc                                                               MIT

Every release that ships an AppImage also carries the release asset appimage-runtime-sources-<version>.tar.gz: the
source of the runtime at tag 20251108 (its build scripts and the libfuse patch) and fuse-3.15.0.tar.xz, the libfuse
source the runtime is built from.

yakbd CLI
---------
The packages include the yakbd command-line tool (https://github.com/yakbd/yakbd-cli), MIT-0, from a tagged release
of that repository, with that release's LICENSE and NOTICE next to it (yakbd-cli-LICENSE, yakbd-cli-NOTICE; in the macOS
app in Contents/Resources); the CLI carries Unicode data and third-party names that its NOTICE lists. This
repository contains none of its code.

kbl specification and test data
-------------------------------
qml/schema/kbl.schema.json and the example layouts in tests/data/ (except pinned-minimal-qwerty.kbl.json) are
unchanged copies from https://github.com/yakbd/kbl-spec at commit ba415d58535b13ec1a702d7b16f94d6bd2730223
(MIT-0). The layout data in tests/data/cldr-pt-abnt2.kbl.json is a conversion of CLDR release-49
keyboards/3.0/pt-t-k0-abnt2.xml (https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr) and is under the Unicode License v3
(third_party/licenses/Unicode-3.0.txt), Copyright (c) Unicode, Inc. tests/data/pinned-minimal-qwerty.kbl.json is
the output of `yakbd pin` (0.1.0-preview.2) on minimal-qwerty.kbl.json. qml/templates/new.kbl.json is
minimal-qwerty.kbl.json with its metadata replaced.

Icon
----
qml/icons/yakbd.svg is the project's own drawing (MIT-0). packaging/windows/yakbd.ico (PNG images of 16 to 256 px)
and packaging/macos/yakbd.icns (PNG images of 32 to 1024 px) are renders of that SVG made with Qt's SVG renderer;
tools/make-icons/ rebuilds them (see its main.cpp).

Other code
----------
The editor's JSON reader and writer, document model and views are its own; no third-party C++ library is
vendored in this repository.
